# CPU-TIME probe, mul. Wall time on a contended machine is unusable (measured
# 2-3x run-to-run drift here); total process CPU time is far more robust,
# because a thread that is descheduled does not accrue CPU time. Subtracting
# the baseline script -- identical but with zero op reps -- removes process
# startup and data generation, leaving the CPU cost of the op alone.
m = reshape(randn(4000000, 1), 2000, 2000)
x = abs(m)
for r = 1 to 60
    x = m .* m
end for
print("{m[0,0]:.4f}")
